useCapability bodySizeHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose bodySizeHandler "Classify request bodies by adapter-reported byte length so tests can confirm http.requestBodyLength's measurement is consistent across POST and PUT and across small/large bodies"
invariant bodySizeHandler "Body length is measured by the adapter before handler dispatch; CByteCount lowers as i64 for the math.greaterThanOrEqualI64 comparison (operands MUST already be i64-shaped, no implicit widening). A zero-byte body is a valid input and reports as `small body` — there is intentionally no guard here because http.requestBodyLength is non-nullable (returns 0, not null)."
warning bodySizeHandler "Same handler is registered against BOTH POST and PUT /reflect/body-size routes — the route table at the top of this file duplicates the verb but uses a single handler to keep size-classification logic in one place; the routeMiddleware list deliberately has one entry for the shared path."

label startBodySizeHandler

