operation sseOneEventHandler
input sseOneEventHandler request HttpRequest
input sseOneEventHandler response HttpResponse
output sseOneEventHandler CSignedInt32
effect sseOneEventHandler write http.response
memory sseOneEventHandler arena request
async sseOneEventHandler no
useCapability sseOneEventHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose sseOneEventHandler "Return one server-sent-event frame (text/event-stream) through the blocking HTTP adapter so tests can verify SSE framing without needing a long-lived connection"
invariant sseOneEventHandler "Current native SSE support is one-shot event-stream FORMATTING, not a long-lived streaming connection — the response is sent and the socket closes. Cache-Control: no-cache is added because intermediaries can otherwise cache an event-stream response, defeating the live-event semantics."
warning sseOneEventHandler "Real SSE clients hold the socket open for many events; this handler returns immediately after one event. Tests that expect server-push behavior need a future long-lived response API (tracked under SYNTAX.md's webServer Partial row)."

label startSseOneEventHandler

