operation gauntletMiddleware
input gauntletMiddleware request HttpRequest
input gauntletMiddleware response HttpResponse
output gauntletMiddleware CSignedInt32
effect gauntletMiddleware read http.request.path
effect gauntletMiddleware write http.response
memory gauntletMiddleware arena request
async gauntletMiddleware no
useCapability gauntletMiddleware httpRequestReader
useCapability gauntletMiddleware httpResponseWriter
purpose gauntletMiddleware "Set diagnostic response headers (X-Gauntlet-Middleware, X-Gauntlet-Path) before each path-scoped route handler runs so the test can verify middleware actually executed and saw the right path"
invariant gauntletMiddleware "Middleware runs synchronously before the route handler in the native dispatcher (semsc.py:2339-2354 wires the middleware pointer into per-route dispatch); returning zero continues to the handler. http.requestPath always returns a non-null pointer for any dispatched request so no guard is needed for middlewareRequestPath."
warning gauntletMiddleware "The middlewareMissingResponseEffect lint rule enforces that any op bound via routeMiddleware declares `write http.response*`. If you split this middleware into a read-only variant that does not write headers, that route's middleware binding will start tripping the lint until you either add a write effect or rethink whether middleware is the right hook."

label startGauntletMiddleware

